    {
      "evidence": "scripts/rollout_project.py, migrate_ci_runner_answers: `if scm_provider is None: raise ValueError(...)` comes before `if \"ci_runner\" in answers or scm_provider != \"github\": return \"skipped\"` and before the target copier.yml check for `ci_runner`. copier.yml declares `scm_provider` with `default: github`, so Copier itself treats an absent answer as github. The new test only asserts the error for a v1.0.1 target with no ci_runner, so it does not cover the older-target or already-migrated cases. The raise should come only after the project is known to be in scope: target asks ci_runner and answers lack ci_runner.",
      "id": "scm-provider-stop-before-applicability",
      "severity": "material",
      "summary": "migrate_ci_runner_answers raises on a missing scm_provider answer before checking whether the preflight applies at all. Every rollout of a project whose answers lack scm_provider now fails, including rollouts to older targets and projects that already record ci_runner. This contradicts the spec ('Older target and GitLab are unaffected') and the design's applicability rule (decision 5)."
    }
